    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "moss-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "moss stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " baby blanket is 75 x 90 cm. Each row works a double crochet into the chain space below and a chain over the dc below. The offset builds a small dimpled grid that is firm but breathable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK cotton is ideal: the tight stitch shows the grid clearly and the fabric washes well. The pattern is one row that repeats all the way to the end. Total yardage is around 360 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "360 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "16 sts x 16 rows = 10 x 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook. Count both the dc and ch-1 spaces together as one stitch unit each for gauge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc (UK) / sc (US): double crochet"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation chain"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 151 (an odd number to set up the staggered repeat)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "turning-chain"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "turning chain"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of ch 1. Dc into 2nd ch from hook. *Ch 1, skip 1 ch, dc into next ch*. Repeat to end. Turn. (75 dc, 75 ch-1 spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 and onward"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 1. Dc into first ch-1 space. *Ch 1, skip 1 dc, dc into next ch-1 space*. Repeat. End with ch 1, dc into last stitch. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Repeat Row 2 until piece measures 90 cm (about 144 rows). Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work one round of dc (UK) around the perimeter: 1 dc into each dc and each ch-1 space along top and bottom, 1 dc into each row end on sides, 3 dc into corners."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Secure tails with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Block to open the grid: pin the damp blanket to the stated dimensions and allow to dry fully."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 30 degrees gentle. Dry flat. The grid opens slightly with washing, which is normal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The waffle stitch throw uses a post-stitch variation of the same grid idea for a deeper texture. Or the linen stitch blanket is the same pattern in a finer weight."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
